\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {5.1}{\ignorespaces Aggregate four-class results from independently evaluated fold configurations. Panel (a) compares macro F1, while Panel (b) shows why the highest-classification equal-weight fusion is not the preferred configuration when confidence is consumed operationally.}}{100}{figure.5.1}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {5.2}{\ignorespaces Pooled row-normalised confusion matrices over the five held-out IEMOCAP sessions ($n=5{,}531$). Rows are true labels and columns are predicted labels; cell values are percentages of the corresponding true-label row. All panels use the same 0--100\% colour scale. Every fitted parameter represented here was estimated without the corresponding test session.}}{100}{figure.5.2}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {5.3}{\ignorespaces Reliability curves from pooled held-out predictions. Each point represents a non-empty equal-width bin of maximum class probability; the dashed diagonal denotes perfect calibration. Panel (a) compares the unimodal systems with predeclared equal fusion, and Panel (b) shows the effect of validation-derived fusion calibration. ECE values in Table~\ref {tab:calibration-tradeoff} use the prespecified 15-bin calculation, while the curves use ten bins for legibility.}}{102}{figure.5.3}%
